diff --git a/crates/rightkit-job-queue/CHANGELOG.md b/crates/rightkit-job-queue/CHANGELOG.md
index e9a217c..aed5186 100644
--- a/crates/rightkit-job-queue/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/crates/rightkit-job-queue/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,5 +1,15 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## 0.3.3 (unreleased)
+
+All additive; a caller that uses none of it behaves as in 0.3.2. Written without running Cargo, CI-only.
+
+- **Outbound request frames are wiped (bogusyogi/rightkit#734).** `EngineClient` (and so `EngineSupervisor`) no longer leaves a request's bytes in memory: the frame is encoded straight into an exactly sized buffer that is zeroed when the writer thread has written it (or the write failed, or the frame was over the limit), and every string in the request `Value` is zeroed as soon as it is encoded. Secrets in an `Init`/`ModelStoreEnsure`-style `params` therefore do not outlive the call. Limits: object keys and numbers inside `Value`, the caller's own copies of `params`, and `EngineSupervisor::set_snapshot` (which keeps its params on purpose to replay them after a restart) are not wiped; pass a secret by `call`, not as a snapshot. New dependency `zeroize` 1.9 (under `protocol`).
+- **`JobError::details` (bogusyogi/rightkit#734).** `JobError::with_details(Value)` / `details() -> Option<&Value>` carry structured data with an error (for example the platform of a `needs_auth`) instead of packing it into the message. `to_json` / `to_json_with` emit it as `"details"` (so it reaches the dispatcher's error frames, a job's stored `error`, and the C ABI error JSON); `EngineClient` reads `error.details` from an engine's error reply back into the `JobError`; it takes part in equality, and a `null` clears it. No `details` key is written when there are none. The sidecar `wire::WireError` type (in `rightkit-sidecar`) is not changed here; this crate builds its error frames as JSON.
+- **Blocking, cancel-aware job lock acquire (bogusyogi/rightkit#721).** `JobLocks::acquire(job_id, timeout) -> JobResult<Option<JobLock>>`, `JobLocks::acquire_cancellable(job_id, timeout, cancel) -> JobResult<LockWait>` (`LockWait::{Acquired, TimedOut, Cancelled}`, `#[non_exhaustive]`), `JobLocks::lock_path(job_id)` and `JobLocks::dir()`. Waiters for one job id in a process queue in arrival order, `cancel` is checked about every 100 ms, and a waiter leaves the queue when it ends. Replaces polling `try_lock` in a sleep loop. `try_lock` is unchanged.
+- **#466:** already in this crate's 0.3.2 notes below (`JobTable`, `jobs_table`, `unique`, `due_column`, `row_revision`); nothing further added.
+- Tests: `tests/job_lock.rs` (acquire, timeout, cancel, arrival order), unit tests in `src/client.rs` (wiping, exact-size encoding, size limit, error `details` parsed from a reply) and `src/error.rs` (`details` in JSON and equality).
+
 ## 0.3.2 (2026-10-17)
 
 All additive; a store, runner or config that uses none of it behaves as in 0.3.2.
